{{!-- A1's lead story with its three companions — beside it when it has a photograph, beneath it
when it does not.

	{{> "home/lead-block" feed=feed}}

	feed    the shared post window from home/window.hbs

The slices are the shared window's, taken with {{#foreach}}'s 1-based inclusive `from`/`to`:
position 1 is the cover, 2 the lead story, 3–5 the companions.

WHAT THIS BAND DOES WITHOUT PHOTOGRAPHS, AND WHY IT HAS TO DO SOMETHING. The columns are 27fr and
20fr of a 1256px content box, so the lead is ~696px wide and its `aspect-[16/10]` photograph is
~435px of the column's height. Ghost lets a post publish with no image and the design draws no
lead without one, so on an image-free publication this band drew a 222px lead beside a 706px rail
— 484px of empty column, measured on the Day-one publication. That is an **Underset**
(CONTEXT.md) and not an **Orphan**: the post is there, the arrangement is not holding it, so the
fix changes the arrangement rather than omitting the band.

Type alone cannot close it, and this was measured rather than guessed: a Day-one post runs about
fifty words, so the h1 step of the scale plus an eighty-word excerpt recovered 56px of the 484.
Hence the arrangement change — with no photograph the lead has no column to be short in. It runs
the width as a type-set standfirst and the companions run three across beneath it, which is 0px.

THE CONDITION IS THE POST'S OWN `feature_image`, NEVER A POST COUNT. A count threshold would
re-set this band the day post eight was published, which is the objection
`docs/adr/0003-the-theme-omits-chrome-it-has-no-content-for.md` records against content
thresholds; a boolean the post carries itself has no such day. It is also why the whole band sits
inside the lead's own {{#foreach}}: the field is on the post, reachable only from inside the
iteration that puts the post in context, so the companions read the window back through
`../feed` — evaluated in the lead's context, so it resolves one frame up, to this partial's own.
The alternative was a `:has(> article img)` variant on the container, which works and makes the
page's geometry depend on a descendant selector nobody would think to look for.

Both branches are inside the image guard, so a publication with photographs renders the drawn
band exactly: the demo homepage is byte-identical at the 1568px capture width, which is what
keeps every Floor where it was.

`grid-cols-[27fr_20fr]` is the design's 1.35:1 written as whole numbers — 27/20 is exactly 1.35,
so this is the same geometry the capture was scored against. --}}
{{#foreach feed from="2" to="2"}}
	<div class="grid items-start gap-11 {{#if feature_image}}lg:grid-cols-[27fr_20fr]{{/if}}">
		<article class="{{post_class}}">
			<a
				href="{{url}}"
				class="text-text block no-underline">
				{{#if feature_image}}
					<img
						src="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}}"
						{{> "image-srcset" image=feature_image sizes="(min-width: 768px) 704px, 100vw"}}
						{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
						class="border-border block aspect-[16/10] w-full rounded-md border object-cover">
				{{/if}}

				{{#primary_tag}}
					<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent mt-[18px] uppercase">{{name}}</p>
				{{/primary_tag}}

				{{!-- The type-set lead takes the h1 step of the scale rather than an arbitrary size, and
				keeps a 26ch measure so a full-width title still sets as a headline rather than as a line
				of running text. --}}
				<h3
					class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2.5 font-medium text-balance {{#if feature_image}}text-[32px] leading-[1.18]{{else}}max-w-[26ch] text-[clamp(2.125rem,3.4vw,2.875rem)] leading-[1.1]{{/if}}">{{title}}</h3>

				{{!-- Without a photograph the standfirst carries the band: the lead step of the scale on a
				46ch measure, and Ghost's own excerpt at 80 words rather than the default 50. --}}
				{{#if feature_image}}
					<p class="text-body text-muted mt-3.5 max-w-[56ch] leading-[1.6] text-pretty">{{excerpt}}</p>
				{{else}}
					<p class="text-lead text-muted mt-4 max-w-[46ch] leading-[1.55] text-pretty">{{excerpt words="80"}}</p>
				{{/if}}

				<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-4 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</p>
			</a>
		</article>

		{{!-- The companions: a vertical rail beside a photographed lead, three across beneath a
		type-set one. The rule moves with them — `border-b` reads as a divider under a stacked row and
		`border-t` as a cap above a row of columns, which is the rule the archive grid's own imageless
		cards carry too. --}}
		<div class="{{#if feature_image}}flex flex-col gap-7{{else}}mt-3 grid gap-x-9 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-3{{/if}}">
			{{#foreach ../feed from="3" to="5"}}
				{{!-- The 116px thumbnail track is declared only when there is a thumbnail to put in it. An
				unconditional track reserved 116px plus its 20px gap in every row of an image-free
				publication — 136px of a 516px column, and the second Underset this band had. --}}
				<article
					class="{{post_class}} border-border max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] grid items-start gap-5 {{#if feature_image}}grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_116px]{{else}}grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)]{{/if}} {{#if ../feature_image}}border-b pb-7{{else}}border-t pt-6{{/if}}">
					<div>
						{{#primary_tag}}
							<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent uppercase">{{name}}</p>
						{{/primary_tag}}

						<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2 text-[21px] leading-[1.26] font-medium">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-text hover:text-accent no-underline">{{title}}</a>
						</h3>

						<p class="text-small text-muted mt-2.5 leading-[1.55]">{{excerpt}}</p>

						<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</p>
					</div>

					{{#if feature_image}}
						<img
							src="{{img_url feature_image size="s"}}"
							{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
							width="116"
							height="88"
							loading="lazy"
							decoding="async"
							class="border-border block h-22 w-[116px] rounded-sm border object-cover">
					{{/if}}
				</article>
			{{/foreach}}
		</div>
	</div>
{{/foreach}}
